1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,608
Before a single model can appear on your
storefront, the app needs somewhere to

2
00:00:04,668 --> 00:00:05,268
store it.

3
00:00:05,172 --> 00:00:07,013
That's what the Setup page is for.

4
00:00:07,073 --> 00:00:09,865
It takes about ten seconds and you only do
it once.

5
00:00:11,075 --> 00:00:13,263
The dashboard's first step points here.

6
00:00:13,323 --> 00:00:18,163
Shopify keeps custom data in things called
metafields, and the theme block reads your

7
00:00:18,223 --> 00:00:19,200
model out of them.

8
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:22,428
If the definitions don't exist, the block
finds nothing.

9
00:00:23,288 --> 00:00:24,691
Open Setup from the nav.

10
00:00:24,751 --> 00:00:29,018
The page is in three parts: the
definitions themselves, what your theme

11
00:00:29,078 --> 00:00:32,370
can actually see, and the two manual steps
that follow.

12
00:00:33,230 --> 00:00:34,992
There are three definitions.

13
00:00:35,052 --> 00:00:40,261
The first, custom dot model underscore 3D,
is a file reference — it points at the

14
00:00:40,321 --> 00:00:40,921
actual .

15
00:00:40,842 --> 00:00:42,473
glb in your Shopify Files.

16
00:00:42,533 --> 00:00:47,678
The second, custom dot viewer underscore
3D underscore config, is JSON and holds

17
00:00:47,738 --> 00:00:50,085
the viewer settings for that product.

18
00:00:50,945 --> 00:00:52,127
The third is different.

19
00:00:52,187 --> 00:00:56,232
It hangs off the shop rather than a
product, and it's a map from every Model

20
00:00:56,292 --> 00:00:59,311
ID in your library to that model's file
URL and settings.

21
00:00:59,371 --> 00:01:03,308
That's what lets you paste an ID into a
page block anywhere on your store.

22
00:01:04,168 --> 00:01:07,275
Each row says Ready, Missing, or No
storefront access.

23
00:01:07,335 --> 00:01:12,143
That last one matters: a definition can
exist and still be invisible to your

24
00:01:12,203 --> 00:01:16,777
Storefront read access is what makes it
readable, and the button below fixes it

25
00:01:16,837 --> 00:01:17,437
either way.

26
00:01:18,282 --> 00:01:20,568
So: click Create slash fix definitions.

27
00:01:20,628 --> 00:01:25,381
It creates anything missing, turns on
storefront access where it's off, and then

28
00:01:25,441 --> 00:01:27,607
immediately syncs your model library.

29
00:01:27,667 --> 00:01:30,194
It's safe to run as many times as you
like.

30
00:01:31,054 --> 00:01:33,813
All three go green, and you get a
confirmation.

31
00:01:33,873 --> 00:01:38,671
Once you've done this, the button relabels
itself to Re-sync model library — same

32
00:01:38,731 --> 00:01:41,190
action, and it stays available on purpose.

33
00:01:42,050 --> 00:01:45,728
Now the most useful panel on the page:
What the theme block can see.

34
00:01:45,788 --> 00:01:49,959
This doesn't check the schema — it reads
the value back, exactly the way your

35
00:01:50,019 --> 00:01:51,114
theme's Liquid would.

36
00:01:51,174 --> 00:01:55,620
That's the difference between a definition
that exists and a library that actually

37
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:56,280
works.

38
00:01:56,810 --> 00:01:59,953
It also prints the Model IDs the
storefront can resolve.

39
00:02:00,013 --> 00:02:04,414
If a page block reports a model as not
found, compare the ID here with the one

40
00:02:04,474 --> 00:02:07,788
you pasted — nine times out of ten they
simply don't match.

41
00:02:08,648 --> 00:02:13,267
If the library comes back empty while you
clearly have models, the panel says so and

42
00:02:13,327 --> 00:02:17,333
tells you what to do — run the button
again, and if it still reads empty,

43
00:02:17,393 --> 00:02:22,067
Shopify's own rejection message is printed
right here so you can act on it or send it

44
00:02:22,127 --> 00:02:22,727
to support.

45
00:02:23,540 --> 00:02:26,756
And if only some models made it, it tells
you the count.

46
00:02:26,816 --> 00:02:31,202
Models without a resolved file URL get
left out — usually because Shopify is

47
00:02:31,262 --> 00:02:32,840
still processing the upload.

48
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:34,887
Open those models and re-save them.

49
00:02:35,747 --> 00:02:40,121
The rest of the page is the two things
only you can do: add the theme block, and

50
00:02:40,181 --> 00:02:41,562
upload models per product.

51
00:02:41,622 --> 00:02:44,000
Both have their own tutorial in this
series.

52
00:02:44,860 --> 00:02:45,486
That's Setup.

53
00:02:45,546 --> 00:02:49,754
Next we'll add the theme block, which is
the piece that actually draws the viewer

54
00:02:49,814 --> 00:02:50,755
on your storefront.
